# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/s7 window (the ship-7 candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/s7 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt and
# ORDER-SHIP.txt have the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules of the two runs.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW AND THE SHIP: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s7-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft and the ship-7 profile baked as the serving default
# (sed -i 's/tp4-s7-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the same in every
# smoke and prefix job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The replay and build steps do not forward the selection (the job reader refuses the keys beside them): they run the base checkpoint.
# A1 (EXACTNESS of the whole candidate, STOP): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s7-audit, the audited twin of the ship-7 candidate: every audit of the
# shipped stack (the K/V page writer, the verify T2 audit, the pre-stage audits, the multi-user SDPA launch, the vglue, conv-gates and octo-lever audits, the 13x10 grids,
# the host tier with every instrument on, the carry's audit, the hand-off's audit), W3 WC with its audit and the adaptive governor (all three passed their card gates in the
# ship-6 window) PLUS the threaded upload and the lookup, on Swift. The ledger trim is NOT in the twin (the audit's judge reads the ledger's points). Tests: warmup; coding;
# np1_live2 and np1_live4; prefill_few_decoders (the governor's shape); concurrent8_drain (every live count from 8 to 1); concurrent8_steady (the octo rounds, required by
# the smoke check on this profile); agent_turns last (about seventy returning turns, and the returning sessions the host tier restores). READ: c2_smoke_check clean (its
# fusion, octo, grid13, WC and governor rules read the container log); every audit line exact=True with entries above 0; octo_judge.py --container-log <container log>
# --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s7-audit clean; NO "audit mismatch", NO "fell back" but the octo block's one WC line, NO "latched off", NO "kv
# shared", no stall. UPLOAD (QWEN_PREFIX_TIER_IO_THREADS=4, QWEN_PREFIX_TIER_VERIFY_THREADS=4): the line "[PINDIAG] prefix: host tier upload on io_threads=4
# io_chunk_blocks=.. verify_threads=4 io_wrapped=1" once, a returning session restored through the threaded IO (the restore line and tier_io_write_blocks above 0 in the
# counters), NO "host tier upload latched off" line and NO "host tier upload fell back" line (a latch is a FAIL: the call was repeated through the serial code, so the
# answers are right and the lever is not working), zero digest failures. ESTIMATE: a 254k restore of about 1 s falls toward 0.4 to 0.6 s, so a returning turn's first token
# (5.4 to 6.5 s) gains under 0.5 s. LEDGER TRIM (QWEN_FAST_ADMISSION_LEDGER_TRIM=1, the candidate only: the audited twins never trim): "[PINDIAG] admission ledger trim: the
# memory ledger ended after the attach" once and no per-rebind bracket lines after the attach. ESTIMATE: nothing on a warm process, about 1.7 s of a 15.4 s burst into a
# fresh process. LOOKUP (QWEN_FAST_LOOKUP_DRAFT=n3m12, the first card run of the lookup anywhere): "[LOOKUP-DRAFT] engaged policy=n3m12" per rebound request (build_ms in
# it: the index build runs on the step thread and stalls every decoding seat; about 0.07 s at the 32,768-token cap, ESTIMATE) and a "[LOOKUP-ROUND]" line per user per
# round. The target verifies every row, so the answers must be EQUAL to the control's; only the tokens a round commits can move. If the container log carries no engaged
# line the engine-core subprocess's output is not reaching it: say so, do not read the arm. The ship-6 reads stand: W3 WC: the "[PINDIAG] tp4 gdn wc engaged" line
# (conv_cores, gate_cores and z_cores above 0) once per engine start that has an M3 block, a "gdn wc audit <n> exact=True" line on the audited twin and no "audit mismatch";
# the octo block (8 users of 8 rows) declines it with ONE "[PINDIAG] tp4 gdn wc fell back reason=8 users (WC takes 2 or 4)" line, which is the design (w3_wc_smoke accepts
# exactly that line); any other "fell back" line fails. GOVERNOR: the install line "[PINDIAG] lever N adaptive: decoders<=2 share=0.9 ttft=120 gap_floor=8" once; every
# scheduler step line carries base=, target= and adaptive=; adaptive=1 exactly on the prefill steps that ran with one or two decoders live (and the base share 0.9, the
# target 120); adaptive=0 and today's 0.5/180 with none or three or more; f_eff never below base (c2_smoke_check.levern_adaptive_problems judges all of it;
# prefill_few_decoders NOT EXERCISED means no step was adaptive). The decode-gap floor (8 s) holds: no gap over it in the decoders of prefill_few_decoders. agent_turns (6
# sessions of 64k, 128k and 200k tokens, 12 returning turns each) is the MAIN JUDGE: the ship-5 window's T1B number (50.36 tok/s aggregate, returning turn first token p50
# 1.46 s, p90 2.33 s) is its baseline. agent_turns8 is EIGHT sessions weighted like production traffic (contexts of 24k to 80k tokens and one of ~200k, about 550k tokens in
# all, mean ~69k against production's ~59k; answers capped at 300 to 1,080 tokens, mean 690 like production's; the same gaps and 12 turns), every seat busy, no new turn
# after 25 minutes, an estimate of 15 minutes: the production load, where WC (2 or 4 users) and the governor (1 or 2 decoders) mostly sit out, so the pair says whether
# anything is LOST there. Compare it with its own control leg, never with agent_turns. Read both legs with `python3 scripts/ci/agent_turns.py report --smoke-log <smoke>
# --container-log <container> --test <name>`: the rates, the TTFT by context bucket, the tokens re-prefilled, the per-live table; the per-turn answer hashes must be EQUAL
# between the legs. Then python3 scripts/ci/sched_report.py <container log>. The audited profile holds about 2.6 GB more DRAM per chip than the unaudited one (the ship-5
# and ship-6 windows' A1 timed out three agent-turn reads on admission holds that T1B did not have; the owner accepted that for ships 5 and 6): a hold line or a client
# timeout on this job is the audit's own weight, not the candidate's, and it is not a stop reason by itself. ANY audit mismatch, a latch, or a stall is NO-GO for the group
# it names and halts the window. NO-GO for the candidate: any text difference against the control, an audit mismatch, a latch or fall-back line of any of the three groups,
# a fall-back line beyond the octo block's one WC line, a floor violation (a decode gap over 8 s), an allocator or admission failure, an eight-live window outside the
# boot-to-boot drift of the control, a loss in the restore pair, an errored or timed-out agent request. A failing lever is taken out by deleting its line from the ship
# entry of scripts/ci/fusion-wp/S7.json (and, for the ledger trim, from the waiver's levers) and regenerating (a new build): QWEN_PREFIX_TIER_IO_THREADS with
# QWEN_PREFIX_TIER_VERIFY_THREADS, QWEN_FAST_ADMISSION_LEDGER_TRIM, QWEN_FAST_LOOKUP_DRAFT. CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the
# container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=...
# (the base cache is not read or written)" once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2]
# checkpoint bound ..." line; the models answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar
# samples every chip once a second through the smoke step; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A rate difference that comes with a different loaded AICLK
# between the arms is the clocks, not the lever. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job
# beside it. Duration (estimate): 61 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s7-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s7-audit
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,np1_live2,np1_live4,prefill_few_decoders,concurrent8_drain,concurrent8_steady,agent_turns
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=110
